---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BUDGET_YEARS, ARCHIVE_YEARS, YEAR_ROLE, yearPath, type BudgetYear } from '../lib/budget-year';
import { changedHeaders, correctionAnchor, quoteList } from '../lib/corrections';
import { publishedSectionHrefs } from '../lib/published-pages';
import { ABOUT_PAGE_TITLE } from '../lib/site.mjs';

// Public Source's edit of Max's text (relayed by Max, 2026-11-17).
const AI_POLICY_URL = 'https://www.publicsource.org/policies/#h-public-source-ai-policy-and-guidelines';
const SEO_HEADLINE = 'How the Pittsburgh Budget Explorer was built and AI’s role';
const SEO_DESCRIPTION = 'The Pittsburgh Budget Explorer turns the city’s proposed 2027 budget PDFs into searchable tables. Here’s how AI helped build it and how to check its numbers.';
const OFFICIAL_BUDGETS_URL = 'https://www.pittsburghpa.gov/City-Government/Finance-Budget/Management-Budget/Budgets-and-Reports';
const OPERATING_PDF_URL = 'https://www.pittsburghpa.gov/files/assets/city/v/1/omb/documents/operating-budgets/2027-mayors-operating-budget.pdf';
const CAPITAL_PDF_URL = 'https://www.pittsburghpa.gov/files/assets/city/v/1/omb/documents/capital-budgets/2027-mayors-capital-budget.pdf';
const SOURCE_CODE_URL = 'https://github.com/Lemali-Consulting/budget-extractor';
const CLAUDE_CODE_URL = 'https://claude.com/claude-code';
const ERRORS_EMAIL = 'rich@publicsource.org';
const AUTHOR_EMAIL = 'max@lemaliconsulting.com';

const [archive] = ARCHIVE_YEARS as (BudgetYear | undefined)[];
// Every year the site carries, newest first, with the corrections (if any) we made to its source PDF.
const yearsWithCorrections = Object.values(BUDGET_YEARS).sort((a, b) => b.year - a.year);
const yearsWithoutCorrections = yearsWithCorrections.filter((y) => y.corrections.length === 0);
const anyCorrections = yearsWithoutCorrections.length < yearsWithCorrections.length;
const link = 'text-ps-blue-600 hover:underline';
---

<Base title="About" ogTitle={SEO_HEADLINE} description={SEO_DESCRIPTION} aboutIntro={false}>
  <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    <a href="/" class="hover:text-ps-blue-600">Home</a>
    <span class="mx-1" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
    <span>About</span>
  </nav>

  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">{ABOUT_PAGE_TITLE}</h1>
  <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 mb-2 max-w-3xl">How the site was built, what role AI played and what you should keep in mind when using it.</p>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-8">By Max Chis</p>

  <div class="prose max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed" data-about-body>
    <section class="mb-10">
      <p class="text-gray-700">
        Pittsburgh’s budget shows how the city plans to spend public money. But if you want to know how much is set aside for a particular department or service, you may have to sift through pages of tables. We built <a href="/" class={link}>this visualization</a> to make those numbers easier to find and compare. We used AI to help write the code. You can read more in <a href={AI_POLICY_URL} class={link}>Public Source’s AI policy</a> about our approach to AI and the safeguards we follow.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ps-blue-900 mb-3">What is the Pittsburgh Budget Explorer?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700">
        The city publishes its budgets as PDF documents including hundreds of pages of tables, narratives and financial data. This project extracts that data from the PDFs and presents it in searchable, sortable and visual formats.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ps-blue-900 mb-3">What role did AI play?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">
        <a href={CLAUDE_CODE_URL} class={link}>Claude Code</a>, an AI coding tool made by Anthropic, was used extensively throughout the project for:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2 mb-4">
        <li>Writing code to extract information from the city’s PDFs</li>
        <li>Debugging the extraction process, tables and layout</li>
        <li>Building the website, including the layout, navigation, search functionality and visualizations</li>
        <li>Drafting labels, short factual descriptions and definitions of budget terms using the city’s budget documents</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-gray-700">
        We gave Claude Code instructions to stick to the budget documents and make its work easy to check. An editor, a developer and a journalist who fact-checked the project reviewed the work. When they found an error, they had Claude Code look for and fix the same problem throughout the site, then checked the fixes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ps-blue-900 mb-3">Important caveats about accuracy</h2>
      <div class="bg-ps-yellow-50 border border-ps-yellow-200 rounded-lg p-5 mb-5">
        <p class="text-ps-yellow-900">
          <span class="font-semibold">This site is not an official City of Pittsburgh publication and hasn’t been reviewed by city officials.</span>
          For authoritative budget figures, always refer to the <a href={OFFICIAL_BUDGETS_URL} class={link}>official budget documents</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">
        Extracting data from PDFs isn’t perfect. Misaligned columns, missing data, inconsistent formatting, negative numbers and footnotes can lead to misinterpretation.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700">
        The section pages on this site include page references that correspond to the original budget documents. If you spot something that looks wrong, you can verify it against the source PDF and email Public Source’s managing editor at <a href={`mailto:${ERRORS_EMAIL}`} class={link}>{ERRORS_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ps-blue-900 mb-3">Source data</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">
        The data for this site comes from:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2 mb-4">
        <li>The <a href={OPERATING_PDF_URL} class={link}>City of Pittsburgh’s proposed 2027 operating budget</a>, covering department budgets, revenue, personnel, grants, trust funds and financial forecasts</li>
        <li>The <a href={CAPITAL_PDF_URL} class={link}>proposed 2027 capital budget</a>, covering infrastructure, facilities, parks and equipment projects.</li>
      </ul>
      {archive && (
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">
          The {archive.label} budget remains browsable in the
          <a href={yearPath({ budgetYear: archive, path: '/operating/' })} class={link}>{archive.year} archive</a>.
        </p>
      )}
      <p class="text-gray-700">
        The extraction code, test suite and website source code are available on <a href={SOURCE_CODE_URL} class={link}>GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10" id="corrections">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ps-blue-900 mb-3">Corrections we made to the source documents</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">
        Now and then, a city budget PDF contains a labeling error that, taken literally, makes this site show wrong or missing figures. Where the evidence is clear, Pittsburgh Budget Explorer corrects the label and says so on the affected table and section page. These corrections are ours, not the city's. The source PDFs are unchanged, and only column headings are relabeled. No dollar amount is altered.{anyCorrections && ' Each entry below shows what the PDF says, what we show instead and why.'}
      </p>

      {yearsWithCorrections.filter((y) => y.corrections.length > 0).map((y) => (
        <div class="mb-6" data-testid="corrections-year" data-year={y.year}>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">{y.label}</h3>
          {y.corrections.map((c) => {
            const { printed, shown } = changedHeaders(c);
            return (
              <article id={correctionAnchor({ year: y.year, id: c.id })} class="mb-4 border-l-4 border-ps-yellow-400 bg-ps-yellow-50 rounded-r-lg px-4 py-3 text-ps-yellow-900 scroll-mt-20" data-testid="correction-entry">
                <h4 class="font-semibold mb-1">
                  {c.section}, page {c.pdfPage} of the full PDF
                </h4>
                <p class="mb-1"><strong>What the PDF says:</strong> the table's year columns are headed {quoteList(printed)}.</p>
                <p class="mb-1"><strong>What we show:</strong> {quoteList(shown)}. The PDF itself is unchanged; the relabeling is ours.</p>
                <p class="mb-1"><strong>Why:</strong> {c.evidence}</p>
                {y.role !== YEAR_ROLE.COMPARISON_ONLY && publishedSectionHrefs(y)[c.sectionSlug] && (
                  <p>
                    <a href={`${publishedSectionHrefs(y)[c.sectionSlug]}#table-${c.tableId}`} class="font-medium underline hover:text-ps-yellow-700">See the corrected table &rarr;</a>
                  </p>
                )}
              </article>
            );
          })}
        </div>
      ))}

      {anyCorrections ? yearsWithoutCorrections.length > 0 && (
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          No corrections were made to the {yearsWithoutCorrections.map((y) => y.label).join(' or the ')} documents.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p class="text-gray-700" data-testid="no-corrections">
          No corrections have been made to any of the budget documents this site carries.
        </p>
      )}
    </section>

    <p class="text-gray-600 italic">
      Max Chis is the founder of Lemali Consulting, a Pittsburgh business that provides software engineering and technical services for local nonprofits and civic institutions, and can be reached at <a href={`mailto:${AUTHOR_EMAIL}`} class={link}>{AUTHOR_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
